#: ../../source/docs/using-the-command-line-interpreter-to-configure-apmcopter.rst:5
#: 2098e5d9532e410daf46dc652da222a3
msgid "Using the Command Line Interface to Configure Copter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-the-command-line-interpreter-to-configure-apmcopter.rst:9
#: 9af343abdd17463a8b1139f688c28b5d
msgid "The CLI is being phased out on all platforms. The features were massively cut down with AC3.1.5 and then it was removed for the APM2 completely anyway with AC3.2. All CLI functions are now available via regular MAVLink commands in the GCSs. This article has been moved to the dev wiki and may be considered deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-the-command-line-interpreter-to-configure-apmcopter.rst:15
#: 775e6a64f6624b0b8cabd033e4d0f5d6
msgid "You don't need to use the Mission Planner to set up Copter (and there are some advanced configuration options not covered by the Mission Planner). You can also use APM's built-in Command Line Interpreter (CLI) over a serial terminal, which will work on any computer and operating system. It is only available via the USB cable; it cannot be used via a Xbee/3DR wireless connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-the-command-line-interpreter-to-configure-apmcopter.rst:22
#: f6229a9b334d4d2d8e0dacffb96193bf
msgid "You will also need to use the CLI for such functions as assigning your preferred flight modes to your RC transmitter's toggle switches. See the menu descriptions below for instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-the-command-line-interpreter-to-configure-apmcopter.rst:26
#: 480373287f3f46879eeaa5edfd4ec45f
msgid "You can enter the CLI by hitting \"Enter\" three times in the Mission Planner Terminal screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-the-command-line-interpreter-to-configure-apmcopter.rst:29
#: 983f4e83600142eaa46713c855e8abab
msgid "When you open it, it will look like this (with a more recent version number of the software displayed):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-the-command-line-interpreter-to-configure-apmcopter.rst:35
#: b312e258038944eb87d8b495da8477e7
msgid "If you're not using Windows, you can also use the Serial Monitor built into Arduino (remember to select the right baud rate and enable CRs as shown here):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-the-command-line-interpreter-to-configure-apmcopter.rst:42
#: d0077af92275414b9e37596d04fe1624
msgid "Once you are in the CLI, you can type \"help\" at any menu and get a full list of available commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-the-command-line-interpreter-to-configure-apmcopter.rst:45
#: 198b69e75cf84efbbd368ec42651050c
msgid "There are three top-level menus: Setup, Test and Logs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/using-the-command-line-interpreter-to-configure-apmcopter.rst:50
#: cc103d6677bf4cf0a626c18bba9d88ea
msgid "Each has sub-menus, whose command can also be seen by typing \"help\" when you are in that section."
msgstr ""

